    {
      "slug": "reddit-snack-bag-clipboard",
      "script": "She owed how much? Every trip to my store, she let her son rip open snack bags, then walked out without paying because kids get a pass. I started keeping every opened bag behind the register: date, item, price. Three weeks in: forty-one dollars in unpaid snacks, taped to a clipboard. Corporate policy bills opened stock to the last customer who touched it, so I called. Loss prevention flagged her rewards account and froze it. Next day, her free coffee redemption got declined at the register, in front of the line. I slid over the clipboard: forty-one dollars, itemized, dated, signed by three different cashiers. Very artisanal accounting. She paid cash, to the penny. Now she hasn't let her son open so much as a straw wrapper since. What finally closed the snack bar?",
      "editor_note": "Punched up to a four-word question hook, tightened the clipboard escalation, added one dry accounting aside, and landed on the snack-bar reversal while preserving every number, entity, shot phrase, and query."
    },
    {
      "slug": "reddit-not-staff-microwave",
      "script": "Discount from whom? I was buying paint when a woman in a motorized cart cut me off and demanded fifty percent off a dented microwave box, insisting my navy jacket meant I worked there. I told her twice I didn't. She followed me down two aisles, demanding a manager. Apparently the jacket promoted me. So I walked her to the actual customer service desk, said she needed a price match, and left. Turns out the real employee recognized her instantly—same routine every few weeks, different store, same dented-box excuse. Corporate flagged her account after loss prevention pulled the footage from three locations in one month. Now every associate in that chain has her photo taped inside the register drawer. I still don't work there. I paint my garage in peace. What got her banned from four stores in the county?",
      "editor_note": "Punched up to a three-word question hook, compressed the mistaken-employee escalation, added one dry jacket aside, and landed on the four-store ban while preserving every number, entity, shot phrase, and query."
    }
